To find sum of digits of a number:

Get last digit using % 10

Add it to sum

Remove last digit using / 10

Repeat until number becomes 0

Example:

Number = 123
Digits: 3, 2, 1
Sum = 3 + 2 + 1 = 6

✅ C Program: Sum of Digits
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int n, sum = 0, digit;

    printf("Enter a number: ");
    scanf("%d", &n);

    while (n > 0) {
        digit = n % 10;
        sum = sum + digit;
        n = n / 10;
    }

    printf("Sum of digits is %d", sum);

    return 0;
}

🔍 Example Output
Enter a number: 456
Sum of digits is 15

🧩 Trick to Remember the Logic
"MOD → ADD → DIV → REPEAT"

% 10 → get last digit

+ → add to sum

/ 10 → remove last digit

repeat till 0

